<title>USA: Tripos, Panlabs in drug research deal.</title>
<headline>Tripos, Panlabs in drug research deal.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1996-09-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tripos Inc and Panlabs Inc, a division of MDS Health Group, said Monday they finalized a $1.5 million one-year deal with Bristol-Myers Squibb Co to develop drug leads.</p>
<p>Under the agreement, Tripos and Panlabs will design and synthesize focused libraries of chemical compounds that will be used by Bristol-Myers Squibb in its screening efforts, they added.</p>
<p>Panlabs and Tripos joined in mid-1995 in a collaboration to offer services in drug discovery to pharmaceutical, biotechnology and chemical research organizations.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk - 312-408-8787</p>
</text>
